<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  ITA-6 : 6-DOF spherical-wrist manipulator, with parallel-jaw gripper.

  GENERATED by examples/ita6/design_ita6.py : do not hand-edit; re-run the
  script. Link lengths are the winner of a 6x6 design sweep scored on
  caliper's own reachability / manipulability / limit-margin analysis over a
  150 x 240 x 160 mm table-top work zone.

  KINEMATICS (canonical spherical-wrist 6R; every joint origin rpy = 0):
    J1 yaw    axis Z at z = 0.125 m
    J2 pitch  axis Y  (shoulder)      L2 = 0.16 m to the elbow
    J3 pitch  axis Y  (elbow)         L3 = 0.19 m to the wrist centre
    J4 roll   axis Z  |
    J5 pitch  axis Y  +-  these three axes intersect at the WRIST CENTRE
    J6 roll   axis Z  |
    tcp_mount fixed, +0.1 m -> TCP (the frame IK and the task address)
  Reach, base axis -> TCP, arm extended: 0.45 m.

  MASS MODEL : composed analytically from a bill of materials, not guessed:
    aluminium 6061 tube/plate  rho = 2700 kg/m^3   (walls modelled as real walls)
    PLA-CF printed shells      rho = 1240 kg/m^3  (hollow geometry, solid wall)
    steel shafts/screws        rho = 7850 kg/m^3
    NEMA17 0.3 kg | NEMA14 0.14 kg | NEMA11 0.07 kg
    strain wave 0.13 kg | planetary 0.16/0.06/0.03 kg
  Each <inertial> is the parallel-axis sum of those primitives about the link
  COM : valid by construction, which is why A002 passes without tuning.

  DRIVETRAIN -> <limit> (tau_out = tau_motor * ratio * efficiency):
    J1 NEMA17 0.50 N.m x 30:1 belt+planetary x 0.80 -> 12 N.m, 2.433 rad/s
    J2 NEMA17 0.50 N.m x 30:1 strain wave    x 0.80 -> 12 N.m, 2.433 rad/s
    J3 NEMA17 0.50 N.m x 30:1 strain wave    x 0.80 -> 12 N.m, 2.433 rad/s
    J4 NEMA14 0.22 N.m x 20:1 planetary      x 0.75 -> 3.3 N.m, 3.65 rad/s
    J5 NEMA14 0.22 N.m x 20:1 planetary      x 0.75 -> 3.3 N.m, 3.65 rad/s
    J6 NEMA11 0.09 N.m x 14:1 planetary      x 0.75 -> 0.945 N.m, 5.214 rad/s

  Every <collision> is also the <visual>: the shape the doctor lints, the shape
  MuJoCo integrates and the shape the render shows are one object.
-->
<robot name="ita6">

